vmlab: hidden, the display keeps a size of its own; shown, it takes the window's pixels

REIMS_VGPU_WINDOW_HIDDEN_MODE=1920x1080: while no window shows (window-shown-and-hidden-on-
request), the display's mode is that size whatever the window's, so a Mac started for an agent
keeps the pixels its clicks expect. It is pinned as a size nobody measured, so a window shown
again keeps it until the window fills its screen for PIN_SETTLE and pins its own pixels
(REIMS_VGPU_WINDOW_MODE=first, window-pinned-mode): a guest pixel to a screen pixel, no bars, no
scaling. Before, a Mac started hidden had MODE=1920x1080 for good, and the maximized window
(1920x1048) scaled it down between bars. Hidden again, the mode goes back to the hidden size.
The lab's mac26.sh sets it for every window, beside MODE=first.
